  "caveats": [
    "Censored rows (all measurements right- or left-censored) carry no numeric y and are dropped. They are disproportionately inactive compounds, so every fit is on the potent side of the cohort; the dropped share is reported per endpoint.",
    "Matched delta pairs use ligand_main_fragment, i.e. the loose key: the organic ligand is held fixed but counterions/co-ligands may differ. This is the same estimand as MSRS-1's loose sensitivity analysis, not the strict single-variable substitution.",
    "ECFP4 has no explicit metal, so the metal enters only through the metal block. That is the intended metal-aware design, but it means the model cannot represent coordination geometry.",
    "The additive model's delta is ligand-independent by construction; its sign accuracy is therefore a constant per metal pair and is reported as the null, not as a fitted result."
  ]
